            (today: “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"}> chromatic homotopy theory
            ”).
          %p Consists of three lectures, each meant to be readable on their own, and there is overlap in topics. It’s part III that begins with an actual introduction to stable homotopy theory, and so the beginner might prefer to start reading with Part III. Also notice that on p. 87 it says that the material there in part II is to be regarded as superseding part I.
          %p A very detailed and readable account based on these lectures:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochmann"}> Stanley Kochmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
